---
description:Safe loading indicator guidelines
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---
S  Safe loading indicator guidelines:

  - Prefer local loading state:
    - Use StatefulBuilder or local state for self-contained loaders.
    - Avoid depending on parent BuildContext for loading state updates.

  - Capture context-dependent objects early: 
    - Store navigator, scaffoldMessenger, etc. at the start of async methods.
    - Use these stored refs later instead of reusing context.

  - Prefer overlays for persistent loaders:
    - Use OverlayEntry for global/long-running loaders instead of showDialog.
    - Manually insert/remove overlay entries.

  - Use a global LoadingService when needed:
    - Manage global loading state via a service (e.g. Stream/ValueNotifier).
    - Widgets listen to this state instead of passing BuildContext around.

  - Always check mounted before UI updates:
    - After async operations, do:
        if (!mounted) return;
        setState(...);
    - Return early if widget is no longer mounted.

  - Prefer inline UI feedback:
    - Use in-place spinners/placeholder widgets instead of full-screen dialogs
      when possible.

  - Ensure cleanup of loaders:
    - Use whenComplete()/then() to hide loaders even on errors.
    - Example:
        myAsyncOperation().whenComplete(() => LoadingOverlay.hide());

  - Separate UI from business logic:
    - Business logic returns results; UI decides when/how to show loaders.
    - Use Provider/other state management for loading flags where appropriate.